  "notes": [
    "Preregistered promotion requires combined pooled and Standard10 deltas nonnegative, at least 3/4 combined anchors nonnegative, both combined seats nonnegative, each lineage pooled delta nonnegative, exact raw/checkpoint evidence, and both Standard10 drift audits pass. A null result at this tiny single-step dose is insufficient to reject long-horizon conflict-aware training.",
    "Seed1 completed normally: pooled -1.1627 +/-3.6175 bb/100, 2/4 anchors positive, Standard10 -3.7109; directional breadth gate failed but uncertainty is large. Continue preregistered independent Seed2.",
    "Seed2 completed normally: pooled +3.2349 +/-3.8504 bb/100, 3/4 anchors positive, Standard10 +0.8667, both seats positive. Proceed to frozen treatment drift audits.",
    "Both fresh 20k-state Standard10 drift audits PASS: Seed1 mean TV 0.01183 / disagreement 0.0122; Seed2 mean TV 0.01029 / disagreement 0.0111.",
    "No Slumbot calls and no new environment training hands. Raw pair hashes, checkpoint hashes, independent evaluation seeds, and drift raw hashes all verified."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "Across 65,536 untouched greedy evaluation hands, seven-objective treatment versus matched ordinary control was pooled +1.0361 +/-2.6417 bb/100 and positive in both seats, but only 2/4 combined anchors were nonnegative: CFR4 +2.6917, mixed65k +3.4363, iter16 -0.5615, Standard10 -1.4221. Seed1 was -1.1627 while Seed2 was +3.2349. Both fresh 20k-state Standard10 drift audits passed.",
    "conclusion": "The one-step conflict-aware direction is not externally validated for promotion: its positive pooled/seat direction does not replicate by lineage or Standard10/anchor breadth. Because effect sizes are small relative to uncertainty, Seed2 passes all breadth gates, and preservation remains within absolute drift thresholds, this is insufficient-dose/missing-objective evidence rather than rejection of long-horizon conflict-aware learning. Forward KL common descent alone does not reliably preserve the historically important Standard10 greedy execution boundary.",
    "decision": "HOLD_SEVEN_OBJECTIVE_TRAINER_AND_AUDIT_GREEDY_BOUNDARY_OBJECTIVE",
    "next_step": "Before more environment training or another costly matched evaluation, use the immutable audit cohort to compute the Standard10 greedy-margin preservation gradient on both 1M checkpoints. Test whether an eight-objective common descent direction (six opponent-seat rewards, source KL, source greedy boundary) exists and whether the seven-objective update specifically sacrifices that boundary. Only if the mechanism replicates should run a small matched boundary-aware update."
  },
